      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“There are no shoulds, Adam. You can’t force people to be what they aren’t and you can’t just will away your PTSD.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 853
        }
      ],
      "words": 22
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It had occurred to him that morning, in the middle of switching out Mrs. Carpenter’s brake pads, that he could do to Ian",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1220
        }
      ],
      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It could mean failure, but I think it means I’m stuck in the past",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2163
        }
      ],
      "words": 14
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Is it missing or is it a wall?” He sat with that for a moment. It fit. Less like a gap and more akin to something he co",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4633
        }
      ],
      "words": 30
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Grief doesn’t just mean that someone died. It can also mean that you’ve suffered a loss, and you have.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5666
        },
        {
          "text": "“You’ve had a loss of innocence. Your scars aren’t just physical, they’re psychological.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5782
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“No one can be miserable covered in kittens.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6199
        },
        {
          "text": "“Which you are not. When you find your moment, hold it close. Make it last as long as you can.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6305
        }
      ],
      "words": 29
    }
